<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8" />
  <meta name="generator" content="Adobe RoboHelp 2022" />
  <meta name="topic-comment" content="A paragraph describing how collision events with multiple objects are treated where the objects are part of a parent child relationship" />
  <title>Note_Collision_Event_Parent_Child</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../css/default.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <p>Note that for every instance collided with, only one collision event is triggered. When you add multiple collision events to an object, one with a parent object and the other with the child of that object, then only the collision event with the child object is run. If no collision event with the child object exists, but one or more with a parent object do, the collision event with the first parent object going up in the parent-child chain is run.</p>
</body>
</html>